{
  "status": "STABLE",
  "core_findings": [
    "All four categories show positive sampled training separation across 10,317–15,963 valid positions: mean margins are 5.0024–7.6725 and negative-win rates are 1.14%–4.42%. Industrial_and_Scientific is weakest, particularly for items with 1–4 training interactions (7.41% negative wins; 1,580 positions).",
    "All four execution audits report passing; displayed same-tensor readout checks have zero error, and displayed independent-forward checks pass tolerance. Development and held-out diagnostic calibration each show 12 witnessed detections across four categories, passing unchanged controls, and no reported survivors, inactive or invalid mutations; coverage remains limited to three operator families."
  ],
  "key_implications": [
    "Embedding scores near 0.5 indicate little average directional alignment among 2,048 sampled real-item embeddings per category; they do not measure recommendation diversity.",
    "Sampled training discrimination is working, with relatively weaker separation for infrequent Industrial_and_Scientific items; these measurements do not establish validation performance or generalization.",
    "Temporal summaries identify 200 selected users per category but omit effect estimates, leaving temporal and ranking effects unavailable here; strict checkpoint and exported-predictor parity also remain unestablished."
  ],
  "evidence": {
    "headline_metrics": {
      "four_category_embedding_collapse_range": [0.5041, 0.5089],
      "four_category_negative_win_rate_range": [0.0114, 0.0442],
